{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>But the Levites shall camp around the Tabernacle of the Testimony, so that there be no wrath</b> – Even though this was stated regarding the Tabernacle while it was among the banners in the wilderness, it is a commandment for the generations also in the Temple, for from here the watches (mishmarot) were instituted. And the reason of \"and the Levites shall keep the charge of the Tabernacle of the Testimony\" is that they shall guard it at night and walk around the Tabernacle, as they said (Sifrei Korach 116): the priests guard from within and the Levites from without, and all of them are like guards for the head of the King. Thus we learned in the baraita of thirty-two middot: a matter that is not explained in its place but is explained in another place, how so, etc. Similar to it: \"The families of the sons of Kohath shall camp\" etc. (Numbers 3:29), \"The families of the sons of the Gershonite shall camp on the side of the Tabernacle westward\" (ibid. v. 23), \"and the head of the father's house for the families of the Merari\" etc. \"on the side of the Tabernacle they shall camp northward\" (ibid. v. 35). But we have not heard that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded him to make his sons into twenty-four watches. And where have we heard it? \"These were their reckonings for their service, to come into the house of YHWH, according to their ordinance, by the hand of Aaron their father, as YHWH, Elohim of Israel, had commanded him\" (1 Chronicles 24:19). We learn that this commandment was in the hand of Moses and Aaron. And we further learned in tractate Tamid (ch. 1, mishnah 1): in three places the priests guard in the Temple. And they said in its Gemara (26a): whence these matters? Abaye said, for the verse says (Numbers 3:38): \"And those who camp before the Tabernacle eastward, before the Tent of Meeting eastward, Moses,\" and then \"Aaron and his sons, keeping the charge of the Sanctuary\" – Aaron in one place and his sons in two places, etc., as is found there. We learn that they are commandments for the generations and are not for the Tabernacle alone, and the verses in Chronicles (1 Chron. 23–26) are explicit regarding the matter of the watches and the entire arrangement."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The abbreviation כ״ד (before משמרות) is resolved as twenty-four, referring to the twenty-four priestly watches."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:23.573124178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}